==Old English==
===Etymology===
West Germanic, of unknown origin: cognate with Old Frisian ''[[knecht]]'', Old Saxon ''[[knecht]]'', Old High German ''[[kneht]]'' (German ''[[Knecht]]'', Dutch ''[[knecht]]'').

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|/knɪçt/}}

===Noun===
'''cniht''' {{m}} (''plural'' '''[[cnihtas]]''')

# [[boy]], [[youth]]
# (male) [[servant]], [[attendant]]
# male of high military rank, ranking below a [[baron]], usually previously having worked as a [[page]] or [[squire]]

===Descendants===
*English [[knight]] / [[Knight]]

